.TH OYAMA-HRT-APP 1 "2026-11-01" "Oyama's HRT Tracker 0.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
oyama-hrt-app \- desktop application for tracking hormone replacement therapy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B oyama-hrt-app
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B oyama-hrt-app
is a native Qt desktop application for tracking hormone replacement therapy
doses, lab results, and pharmacokinetic curves. All data is stored locally in
an encrypted PostgreSQL database managed by the application. The default build
uses Qt 6.4 or newer; a Qt 5.15.2 compatibility build is available.
.PP
The application provides a graphical interface for:
.IP \(bu 2
Recording and editing dose events (injections, patches, gels, oral, etc.)
.IP \(bu 2
Viewing pharmacokinetic curves (E2, CPA, T) over time
.IP \(bu 2
Importing and exporting encrypted backups
.IP \(bu 2
Managing settings, preferences, and calibration data
.PP
On first run, the application guides the user through vault setup, including a
24-word BIP39 recovery phrase. The PostgreSQL backend is configured with
.BR "oyama-hrt-cli db setup" ;
the shell cannot load data until a backend is available. Existing vaults keep
their original recovery phrase.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-self-test
Boot the shell with the offscreen platform and verify that the vault gate
covers and disables the application shell while the vault is not unlocked.
.TP
.B \-\-screenshot PATH
Render a screenshot to
.IR PATH .
.TP
.B \-\-page NAME
Select the initial page for a screenshot run.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/oyama-hrt/config
Application configuration and selected PostgreSQL backend. Defaults to
.IR ~/.config/oyama-hrt/config .
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/oyama-hrt/
Application data directory, including the default managed cluster at
.IR pgdata .
.SH SECURITY
The application locks the vault after 15 minutes of inactivity and on quit,
zeroing the in-memory data encryption key. The
.I full
security profile adds a panic lock, a best-effort capture guard, and the
.BR oyama-keyd
reference key-isolation deployment. These features have documented limits; see
.IR docs/security/ .
.SH SUPPORT
Support is self-service.
.B Do not contact the developer for support.
Read this man page, the documentation in
.I docs/
(start with
.IR docs/README.md
and
.IR docs/SUPPORT.md ),
and the GitHub wiki first; only open a GitHub issue if those do not answer your
question.
.PP
